window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-007.json",{"day":7,"title":"Looking Past the Royal Portrait","targetWords":[{"word":"prince","gloss":"王子","context":"The museum’s new exhibition began with a portrait of a prince, but its central subject was the person who usually stood outside the frame.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"slim","gloss":"纤细的","context":"The prince’s slim waist, slender neck, and raised chin suggested elegance; a bare wrist showed no sign of physical labor.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"chest","gloss":"胸","context":"An illustration of a skeleton identified each limb and the chest, while another located the liver, kidney, and stomach, alongside a study of breast tissue.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"theirs","gloss":"他们的","context":"“The picture is hers,” the guide said of the woman’s own account; “the official praise is theirs.” Reading both required judgment rather than a quick gut reaction.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"bare","gloss":"裸露的","context":"The prince’s slim waist, slender neck, and raised chin suggested elegance; a bare wrist showed no sign of physical labor.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"eyesight","gloss":"视力","context":"The child nudged a cat’s tail gently with one toe and worried that weak eyesight would prevent him from recognizing his father.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"stomach","gloss":"胃","context":"An illustration of a skeleton identified each limb and the chest, while another located the liver, kidney, and stomach, alongside a study of breast tissue.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"virgin","gloss":"处女","context":"Nearby, a saintly “virgin” in a painting looked serene, but a raised eyebrow and the sitter’s surviving letters suggested a lively personality.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"breast","gloss":"乳房","context":"An illustration of a skeleton identified each limb and the chest, while another located the liver, kidney, and stomach, alongside a study of breast tissue.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"neck","gloss":"脖子","context":"The prince’s slim waist, slender neck, and raised chin suggested elegance; a bare wrist showed no sign of physical labor.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"aunt","gloss":"姑","context":"In the final room, an aunt recalled holding a child on her lap while the family awaited news of its missing kin.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"bald","gloss":"秃头的","context":"A bald uncle and a grieving widow occupied the background.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"legacy","gloss":"留下的遗产","context":"The royal legacy was well documented; the ordinary carrier’s experience survived in a niece’s notebook.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"limb","gloss":"肢体","context":"An illustration of a skeleton identified each limb and the chest, while another located the liver, kidney, and stomach, alongside a study of breast tissue.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"beard","gloss":"胡须","context":"A bride with a smooth cheek sat beside an heir whose beard emphasized maturity.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"elder","gloss":"长者","context":"An elder later recorded his story, including the months when his family did not know whether he was a hostage or simply missing.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"gut","gloss":"直觉","context":"“The picture is hers,” the guide said of the woman’s own account; “the official praise is theirs.” Reading both required judgment rather than a quick gut reaction.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"peasant","gloss":"农民","context":"A peasant had carried the portrait during a journey through hostile territory and become a captive after the party was attacked.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"tail","gloss":"尾巴","context":"The child nudged a cat’s tail gently with one toe and worried that weak eyesight would prevent him from recognizing his father.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"juvenile","gloss":"年轻的","context":"A maid received a nickname instead of a proper name, while a juvenile servant was valued chiefly for obedience.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"thumb","gloss":"拇指","context":"By contrast, the carrier’s worn palm, injured thumb, and swollen ankle appeared only in the written account.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"captive","gloss":"俘虏","context":"A peasant had carried the portrait during a journey through hostile territory and become a captive after the party was attacked.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"cheek","gloss":"脸颊","context":"A bride with a smooth cheek sat beside an heir whose beard emphasized maturity.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"dwarf","gloss":"身材矮小者","context":"One court entertainer was described only as a dwarf, although letters showed his skill as a musician.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"eyebrow","gloss":"眉毛","context":"Nearby, a saintly “virgin” in a painting looked serene, but a raised eyebrow and the sitter’s surviving letters suggested a lively personality.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"knee","gloss":"膝盖","context":"Visitors began to inspect the knee and elbow positions in other portraits with new curiosity.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"liver","gloss":"肝脏","context":"An illustration of a skeleton identified each limb and the chest, while another located the liver, kidney, and stomach, alongside a study of breast tissue.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"hers","gloss":"她的","context":"“The picture is hers,” the guide said of the woman’s own account; “the official praise is theirs.” Reading both required judgment rather than a quick gut reaction.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"kidney","gloss":"肾","context":"An illustration of a skeleton identified each limb and the chest, while another located the liver, kidney, and stomach, alongside a study of breast tissue.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"skeleton","gloss":"骨架","context":"An illustration of a skeleton identified each limb and the chest, while another located the liver, kidney, and stomach, alongside a study of breast tissue.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"bride","gloss":"新娘","context":"A bride with a smooth cheek sat beside an heir whose beard emphasized maturity.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"flesh","gloss":"肉体","context":"Yet the curator explained that attention to flesh had helped artists move beyond idealized forms.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"lap","gloss":"膝上","context":"In the final room, an aunt recalled holding a child on her lap while the family awaited news of its missing kin.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"nickname","gloss":"昵称","context":"A maid received a nickname instead of a proper name, while a juvenile servant was valued chiefly for obedience.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"niece","gloss":"侄女","context":"The royal legacy was well documented; the ordinary carrier’s experience survived in a niece’s notebook.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"slender","gloss":"细长的","context":"The prince’s slim waist, slender neck, and raised chin suggested elegance; a bare wrist showed no sign of physical labor.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"elbow","gloss":"手肘","context":"Visitors began to inspect the knee and elbow positions in other portraits with new curiosity.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"layman","gloss":"外行","context":"For a layman, the detailed drawings could be unsettling.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"palm","gloss":"手掌","context":"By contrast, the carrier’s worn palm, injured thumb, and swollen ankle appeared only in the written account.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"waist","gloss":"腰","context":"The prince’s slim waist, slender neck, and raised chin suggested elegance; a bare wrist showed no sign of physical labor.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"widow","gloss":"寡妇","context":"A bald uncle and a grieving widow occupied the background.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"heir","gloss":"继承人","context":"A bride with a smooth cheek sat beside an heir whose beard emphasized maturity.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"kin","gloss":"亲属","context":"In the final room, an aunt recalled holding a child on her lap while the family awaited news of its missing kin.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"maid","gloss":"女佣","context":"A maid received a nickname instead of a proper name, while a juvenile servant was valued chiefly for obedience.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"naked","gloss":"裸体的","context":"A naked figure was not always an invitation to desire; sometimes it was an effort to understand how a human being stood, breathed, and carried weight.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"toe","gloss":"脚趾","context":"The child nudged a cat’s tail gently with one toe and worried that weak eyesight would prevent him from recognizing his father.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"wrist","gloss":"手腕","context":"The prince’s slim waist, slender neck, and raised chin suggested elegance; a bare wrist showed no sign of physical labor.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"ankle","gloss":"踝","context":"By contrast, the carrier’s worn palm, injured thumb, and swollen ankle appeared only in the written account.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"chin","gloss":"下巴","context":"The prince’s slim waist, slender neck, and raised chin suggested elegance; a bare wrist showed no sign of physical labor.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"hostage","gloss":"人质","context":"An elder later recorded his story, including the months when his family did not know whether he was a hostage or simply missing.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"The museum’s new exhibition began with a portrait of a prince, but its central subject was the person who usually stood outside the frame. A peasant had carried the portrait during a journey through hostile territory and become a captive after the party was attacked. An elder later recorded his story, including the months when his family did not know whether he was a hostage or simply missing. The royal legacy was well documented; the ordinary carrier’s experience survived in a niece’s notebook.","zh":"博物馆的新展览以王子的肖像开场，但真正的主角是通常站在画面之外的人。一位农民曾在穿越敌对地区时搬运这幅画像，队伍遭袭后，他被俘虏了。一位长者后来记录他的经历，其中包括家人不知道他究竟被扣作人质还是失踪的那几个月。王室的遗产有详尽文献，而普通搬运者的经历仅保存在侄女的笔记本里。"},{"en":"A conservator explained how painters made power visible. The prince’s slim waist, slender neck, and raised chin suggested elegance; a bare wrist showed no sign of physical labor. By contrast, the carrier’s worn palm, injured thumb, and swollen ankle appeared only in the written account. The difference was not a reliable measure of character. It reflected who commissioned an image, who posed, and whose body was considered worth preserving. Visitors began to inspect the knee and elbow positions in other portraits with new curiosity.","zh":"修复师解释画家如何让权力显现。王子纤细的腰身、修长的脖颈和抬起的下巴显示优雅，露出的手腕没有体力劳动的痕迹。搬运者磨损的手掌、受伤的拇指和肿胀的脚踝，则只出现在文字里。这种差别不能可靠地说明品格，而反映了谁委托画像、谁摆姿势，以及谁的身体被认为值得留存。游客开始带着新的好奇心，观察其他肖像中膝盖和手肘的姿势。"},{"en":"The exhibition compared historical art with an early anatomy book. An illustration of a skeleton identified each limb and the chest, while another located the liver, kidney, and stomach, alongside a study of breast tissue. For a layman, the detailed drawings could be unsettling. Yet the curator explained that attention to flesh had helped artists move beyond idealized forms. A naked figure was not always an invitation to desire; sometimes it was an effort to understand how a human being stood, breathed, and carried weight. The distinction depended on context.","zh":"展览把历史艺术与早期解剖学著作进行比较。一幅骨骼图标出四肢与胸部，另一幅则标示肝、肾和胃，旁边还有乳房组织的研究图。对外行而言，这些细致图像可能令人不安。但策展人解释，关注真实肉体帮助艺术家突破理想化形式。裸体并不总是为了诱发欲望，有时只是试图理解人怎样站立、呼吸和承重。两者的区别取决于语境。"},{"en":"Other paintings revealed how roles could overwhelm individuals. A bride with a smooth cheek sat beside an heir whose beard emphasized maturity. A bald uncle and a grieving widow occupied the background. A maid received a nickname instead of a proper name, while a juvenile servant was valued chiefly for obedience. One court entertainer was described only as a dwarf, although letters showed his skill as a musician. Labels that seemed convenient to their authors could conceal the full lives of those they named.","zh":"其他画像揭示了角色如何遮蔽个人。脸颊光洁的新娘坐在继承人旁边，后者用胡须强调成熟。背景里是一位秃头叔叔和悲伤的寡妇。女佣只有绰号，没有正式名字；年轻侍从则主要因顺从受到重视。一位宫廷艺人仅被描述为身材矮小者，尽管书信证明他擅长音乐。对记录者方便的标签，却可能掩盖被记录者完整的人生。"},{"en":"In the final room, an aunt recalled holding a child on her lap while the family awaited news of its missing kin. The child nudged a cat’s tail gently with one toe and worried that weak eyesight would prevent him from recognizing his father. Nearby, a saintly “virgin” in a painting looked serene, but a raised eyebrow and the sitter’s surviving letters suggested a lively personality. “The picture is hers,” the guide said of the woman’s own account; “the official praise is theirs.” Reading both required judgment rather than a quick gut reaction. Visitors were invited to distinguish what they could see from what they merely assumed, a practice that made the exhibition relevant far beyond the study of paintings or royal families.","zh":"最后一个展厅里，一位姑妈回忆，一家人等待失踪亲人的消息时，她把孩子抱在膝上。孩子用脚趾轻轻碰猫尾巴，又担心视力差会让自己认不出父亲。旁边一幅画中的“圣洁处女”神态宁静，但微微扬起的眉毛和模特留下的书信显示，她其实个性活泼。讲解员谈到这位女性自己的叙述时说：“这是属于她的画面，官方赞美则属于他们。”同时阅读两种记录，需要判断，而不是匆忙凭直觉下结论。游客被邀请区分自己确实看见的内容与仅仅假定的内容，让展览的意义远远超出绘画或王室研究。"}],"previous":6,"next":8});
